/* AgentKit user-facing messages (en)
 *
 * The strings that tell the user what went wrong: a refused write, a parse that
 * failed, validation that did not pass. Core and Surfaces produce them and look
 * them up with L.t(key, "中文原文", table: .messages); the second argument is the
 * literal that shows when the table is missing, so it must stay verbatim.
 *
 * Both tables must carry exactly the same key set — Tests/main.swift asserts it.
 * %@ is a string argument and %d an integer argument, filled in by
 * String(format:). A key never carries an argument, and the two languages must
 * use the same placeholders in the same order.
 */

